Drawing Notes\P\P1.^IAl Laith Project Services LLC Copyright\PThis drawing is the copyright of Al Laith Project Services LLC. No unauthorised use, copy or disclosure is to be made and it is to be returned upon request.The drawing is supplied subject 
  3
to\Pthe company's standard conditions as applicable. Al Laith Project Services LLC reserves the right\Pto amend drawing details and material components subject to stock availability.\P\P2.^IBasis of Design\PThis drawing has been prepared from informa
  3
tion supplied to us by, or on behalf of the Client, who should check that we have correctly interpreted his requirements and that all loadings, dimensions, details, erection and striking sequences etc. are as required and practicable.\P\PThis drawing
  3
 has been prepared in accordance with Al Laith Project Services LLC Equipment Data Sheets.\P^I\P3.^IApplied Loads where applicable (unless otherwise indicated).\P\PPublic Platforms 5.0kN/m²\P\PPublic Seating Grandstands 5.0kN/m² or as per Table 7.1 I
  3
mposed Uniformly Distributed Loads (from BS EN 1991-1-1 and UK National Annex)\P^I\PWind loads where applicable, have been calculated in accordance with Al Laith Project Services LLC\PWind Management Policy.\PMax. Design Wind Speed of 25m/s for outdo
  3
or events has been considered.\P\P4.^IFoundations/Supports\PUnless otherwise noted, sole boards or other means of spreading the imposed loads are supplied by\PAl Laith Project Services LLC. Where Al Laith Project Services LLC equipment is supported, 
  3
suspended, anchored or tied to an existing structure or the ground, the Client must ensure that the structure or ground is adequate to safely support the additional imposed loads.\P\P5.^ITying & Bracing\PThe Client is responsible for ensuring all str
  3
uctures remain adequately tied and/or braced to carry the load and ensure stability. No ties or braces are to be removed or altered in any way without the expressed written authority from Al Laith Project Services LLC. \P\P6.^ICladding\PThe structure
  3
(s) shown on this drawing will have the following type of cladding \P\P\P^I^I\P7.^IBallast for Stability\PTotal ballast, if required, will be confirmed when all loads are verified.\P\P8.^IModification\PNo alteration to components, assembly, loading o
  1
r any other aspect must be made without the expressed written authority from Al Laith Project Services LLC.^I\P\P9.^IRevisions\PThis scheme may require revising upon completion of load calculations or further comments from the Client.
