Drawing Notes\P\P1.^IAl Laith Project Services LLC Copyright\P^IThis drawing is the copyright of Al Laith Project Services LLC. No unauthorised use, copy or disclosure is to ^I^Ibe made and it is to be returned upon request.The drawing is supplied su
  3
bject to the company's standard ^I^Iconditions as applicable. Al Laith Project Services LLC reserves the right to amend drawing details and ^I^I^Imaterial components subject to stock availability.\P\P2.^IBasis of Design\P^IThis drawing has been prepa
  3
red from information supplied to us by, or on behalf of the Customer, who should ^Icheck that we have correctly interpreted his requirements and that all loadings, dimensions, details, erection, ^I^Ipouring and striking sequences etc. are as required
  3
 and practicable.\P\P^IThe following documents have been used to prepare this scheme:-\P\P^ICustomer Drawings:^I^I....................................................................................\P^ICustomer Drawings:^I^I..........................
  3
..........................................................\P^IDesign Brief:^I^I^I^I....................................................................................\P^ICustomer Method Statement:^I...................................................
  3
.................................\P^IOther Information:^I^I^I....................................................................................\P\P^IThis drawing has been prepared in accordance with Al Laith Project Services LLC Equipment Data Shee
  3
ts, \P\P^ITo enable us to complete this drawing, we have allowed for the following:-\P^I.......................................................................................................................................\P^I.......................
  3
................................................................................................................\P^I......................................................................................................................................
  3
.\P^I.......................................................................................................................................\P^IThe Customer is to check and confirm that we have correctly interpreted his requirements.\P^I\P3.^IApplied
  3
 Loads\P^IApplied loads (unless otherwise indicated) where applicable:-\P\P^IAccess^IWorking Lifts^I....................No. @.....................kN/m²\P^I^I^IAdditional Lifts^I....................No. @.....................kN/m²\P^I^I^IHop-Up Bracket
  3
s^I....................No. @.....................kN/m²\P\P^IWind^I^IWind loads where applicable, have been calculated in accordance with BS 6399.\P^I^I^IMax. Design Wind ^IForce.....................kN/m²\P\P4.^ITimber\P^INo timber is supplied by Al L
  3
aith Project Services LLC unless specifically stated. Where Al Laith Project ^I^IServices LLC does not supply, the design & supply of timber is the responsibility of the Customer. \P\P5.^IFoundations/Support\P^IUnless otherwise noted, no sole plates 
  3
or other means of spreading the imposed loads are supplied by\P^IAl Laith Project Services LLC. Where Al Laith Project Services LLC equipment is supported, suspended, ^I^Ianchored or tied to an existing structure or the ground, the Customer must ensu
  3
re that the structure or ground ^Iis adequate to safely support the additional imposed loads.\P\P6.^IModification\P^IThis drawing has been prepared using the Safe Working Loads of the Al Laith Project Services LLC ^I^I^Icomponents ^Ispecified. No alt
  3
eration to components, assembly, loading or any other aspect must be made ^I^Iwithout the expressed written authority from Al Laith Project Services LLC.\P\P7.^ITying & Bracing\P^IThe Customer is responsible for ensuring all structures remain adequat
  3
ely tied and/or braced to carry the load ^Iand ensure stability. No ties or braces are to be removed or altered in any way without the expressed written ^I^Iauthority from Al Laith Project Services LLC. Where Al Laith Project Services LLC is supplyin
  3
g equipment only, ^Ithe supply & fixing of all necessary ties is the responsibility of the Customer.\P\P8.^ITemporary Working Platforms\P^IUnless specifically stated it is considered that any other working platforms (for erection or dismantling ^I^I
  3
^Ipurposes), will be designed, supplied and fitted by the Customer.\P\P9.^IDesign Output\P^IThis drawing should be read in conjunction with :-\P^I........................................................................................................
  3
........................................................................   \P^I...........................................................................................................................................................................
  3
.....\P\P^IUnless indicated otherwise, all loads shown are not factored.\P^IMaximum calculated Leg Load =..........................kN\P^ILift positions and bracing frequency to be as shown.\P\P^IMaximum calculated Tie Load =..........................
  3
.kN\P^ITie Type :-.................................................................\P^ITie spacing to be as shown on drawing.\P\P10.^IEccentricity\P^IAll legs are to be erected plumb and loaded concentrically to the general tolerances given in BS5975
  3
:2019\P\P11.^IObligation, Responsibilities & CDM\P^IThis drawing constitutes Al Laith Project Services LLC Risk Assessment in accordance with Regulation 9,\P^IDuty of Designers of the current CDM Regulations 2015. The elimination of general risk in t
  3
he use of ^I^I^Itemporary works is by use of good practice. Guidance can be found within relevant Codes, HSE publications ^I^Iand Guides.\P^IWherever possible, risk is designed out of this proposal during the design process. \P\P\pxi16.18;***********
